╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ zero_phase_adaptive_kalman_filter                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the simple exponential weighted moving average with an adaptive two-pass filter   │
│                          │ combining (1) a fast Savitzky-Golay style local polynomial fit for zero-phase             │
│                          │ (forward-backward) smoothing that preserves slope/trend, (2) adaptive noise estimation    │
│                          │ via median absolute deviation to auto-tune smoothing strength, and (3) a robust           │
│                          │ trend-consistency step that suppresses spurious slope reversals. The key improvements:    │
│                          │ moving average introduces group delay ~W/2 causing high lag_error (0.38) and false        │
│                          │ reversals (175.4); a locally-fitted polynomial evaluated at the window center has         │
│                          │ near-zero phase delay and preserves polynomial trends exactly, dramatically improving     │
│                          │ lag_error, slope_changes, false_reversals, and correlation simultaneously. Computation is │
