│                          │ lag_error=0.38) with a zero-lag dual-pass filter: forward EMA followed by a backward EMA  │
│                          │ cancels phase delay, and a Savitzky-Golay-style local polynomial fit evaluated at the     │
│                          │ window center preserves slope dynamics and reduces spurious slope changes/false           │
│                          │ reversals. The polynomial fit preserves genuine trends (high tracking accuracy) while the │
│                          │ EMA passes suppress broadband noise, improving smoothness and noise reduction             │
│                          │ simultaneously with minimal added computation (O(W) per sample with precomputed SG        │
│                          │ coefficients via least-squares). The combination (zero-lag EMA cascade + centered         │
│                          │ polynomial fit, blended 50/50) attacks all four objectives: slope-change minimization     │
│                          │ (smooth polynomial fit), lag minimization (backward pass cancels phase), tracking         │
│                          │ accuracy (centered fit follows local trend), false-reversal penalty (noise is heavily     │
│                          │ attenuated before derivative estimation).                                                 │
