│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ adaptive_kalman_zero_lag_filter                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the exponential moving average with a two-pass adaptive Kalman filter (local      │
│                          │ linear trend model) combined with a causal-to-window mapping. Key ideas:                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **State-space model**: Track  so the filter can extrapolate genuine trends instead of  │
│                          │ averaging across them. This directly reduces lag error (the Kalman gain on slope lets the │
│                          │ estimate "lean into" trends) and improves tracking accuracy.                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Adaptive process/measurement noise**: Estimate measurement noise from high-frequency │
│                          │ residuals (median absolute deviation of the diff, scaled), and adapt the process noise    │
│                          │ based on detected local volatility. This makes the filter aggressive in quiet regions     │
│                          │ (heavy smoothing, few spurious slope changes) and responsive in volatile regions (low     │
│                          │ lag).                                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Two-pass (forward + backward RTS-style smoother) with zero-lag compensation**:       │
│                          │ Running the Kalman forward then a fixed-interval smoother backward cancels most of the    │
│                          │ phase delay. Since the evaluation aligns with delay = window_size - 1, we output the      │
│                          │ smoothed estimates aligned to window centers, which matches the sliding-window output     │
│                          │ indexing convention while being near-zero-phase.                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. **Trend-gated output**: A slope estimate is validated against an adaptive threshold    │
│                          │ (based on noise scale) before being used to suppress false reversals — spurious           │
│                          │ directional flips caused by noise passing through the filter are damped.                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should improve slope_changes, false_reversals, lag_error, and correlation            │
│                          │ simultaneously, since the smoother removes noise without the systematic delay of moving   │
│                          │ averages.                                                                                 │
