│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ kalman_savgol_hybrid                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the exponentially-weighted moving average with a two-stage hybrid: (1) a 1D       │
│                          │ Kalman filter with adaptive process noise (larger Q when innovation magnitude suggests    │
│                          │ genuine dynamics change, smaller Q when noise-dominated) to smooth noise with near-zero   │
│                          │ lag, followed by (2) a Savitzky-Golay smoothing filter that fits local low-order          │
│                          │ polynomials, preserving signal trends and slopes without the phase delay of MA filters.   │
│                          │ The Kalman stage makes the output statistically optimal for Gaussian noise; the SG stage  │
│                          │ suppresses slope changes and false reversals. The adaptive Q gate based on normalized     │
│                          │ innovation squared (NIS) keeps responsiveness during genuine trend changes while damping  │
│                          │ noise-induced reversals. Both filters are O(1)/O(window) per sample and causal alignment  │
│                          │ is maintained by the windowing convention already used.                                   │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
