│ patch_name               │ adaptive_kalman_pipeline                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Restructure the filter as a modular pipeline built around an adaptive constant-velocity   │
│                          │ Kalman filter instead of per-window regression. A two-stage architecture is used: (1) a   │
│                          │ warmup stage that initializes the filter state over the first window-1 samples, and (2) a │
│                          │ streaming stage that emits one output per remaining sample, preserving the original       │
│                          │ output length contract. The Kalman filter's process noise is adapted online from the      │
│                          │ innovation (prediction error) magnitude, so it stiffens in quiet regions (heavy           │
│                          │ smoothing, fewer slope changes and false reversals) and loosens quickly at genuine        │
│                          │ dynamics (low lag, high tracking accuracy). Unlike the sliding regression, this is O(1)   │
│                          │ per sample with no per-window fits, giving both better smoothness and efficiency. Helper  │
│                          │ modules (predict, update, adapt) are separated for maintainability.                       │
