│ patch_name               │ robust_quadratic_endpoint_filter                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ Crossover of the three implementations: keep the current program's best idea — robust     │
│                          │ (Huber-reweighted) weighted local regression evaluated at the window's most recent sample │
│                          │ (t=0), which yields excellent correlation (0.92), low lag (0.30) and low avg error (0.32) │
│                          │ — and upgrade the local model from linear to degree-2 (from the first program's           │
│                          │ Savitzky-Golay center-evaluation), so curvature in the non-stationary signal is tracked   │
│                          │ without lag. Key improvements: (1) quadratic basis  fit at t=0 via weighted normal        │
│                          │ equations, still zero-lag since we evaluate at the window end; (2) one Huber reweighting  │
│                          │ pass to suppress noise-induced false reversals; (3) a light 3-tap post-smoothing pass on  │
│                          │ the output to reduce spurious slope changes without adding meaningful phase delay; (4)    │
│                          │ sliding-window reuse of the input array with precomputed time/weight vectors for          │
│                          │ efficiency. The input/output interface (adaptive_filter,                                  │
│                          │ enhanced_filter_with_trend_preservation, process_signal) is unchanged.                    │
