│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ nis_capped_adaptive_q                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Introduce a Normalized Innovation Squared (NIS)-based adaptive process noise mechanism    │
│                          │ with a strict cap. In non-stationary regions the filter needs more process noise to track │
│                          │ genuine dynamics, but uncapped scaling lets noise leak into the velocity (slope) state    │
│                          │ and produces spurious slope churn and false reversals. The recommendation is to scale Q   │
│                          │ by a capped multiplier driven by the NIS: multiplier = 1 + 2 * min(nis, 6)/6, which       │
│                          │ saturates at 3× (keeping genuine dynamics trackable while suppressing noise-driven        │
│                          │ velocity spikes). To compensate for the lower peak adaptivity, q_base is raised slightly  │
│                          │ (q_slope especially), so steady-state tracking is preserved. This directly targets the    │
│                          │ slope_changes (103) and false_reversals (85.4) metrics that dominate the composite score, │
│                          │ while the capped adaptivity keeps lag_error bounded since the filter still opens up       │
│                          │ quickly on genuine regime changes.                                                        │
