│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ hysteresis_reversal_gate                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The current filter achieves excellent lag error (0.19), average error (0.20), correlation │
│                          │ (0.93) and noise reduction (0.59), but suffers from excessive slope churn (337 slope      │
│                          │ changes, 268 false reversals). Prior attempts at simple slope gates (Gen 5: 0.25σ, Gen 8: │
│                          │ 0.5σ) failed because they were permissive, one-sided soft thresholds. The fix is a        │
│                          │ strict, two-sided hysteresis gate applied to the output level path as a final stage:      │
│                          │ estimate slope-noise σ robustly via the MAD of the raw slope sequence, require a sign     │
│                          │ change to exceed 1.2×σ in magnitude, AND require the new direction to persist for 2       │
│                          │ consecutive windows before a reversal is accepted. Otherwise the gated slope keeps its    │
│                          │ previous direction (sign persistence with linear decay toward zero so plateaus remain     │
│                          │ flat). The level is then rebuilt by integrating the gated slopes but blended with the     │
│                          │ original lag-free level estimate (0.75 blend) so the excellent zero-lag property is       │
│                          │ largely preserved while spurious wiggles in the output — which directly drive             │
│                          │ slope_changes, false_reversals, and smoothness — are eliminated. Since the gate only acts │
│                          │ on sign flips, genuine turns exceeding noise σ pass within 2 windows, adding at most a    │
│                          │ small, bounded delay on real reversals only.                                              │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
