│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ capped_nis_kalman_trendlock                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ This design draws on Gen 2's constant-velocity adaptive Kalman filter (excellent          │
│                          │ lag/accuracy) and Gen 3's capped NIS insight. Key changes: (1) process-noise inflation    │
│                          │ from normalized innovation squared is capped at ~4× the baseline (Gen 2 let Q explode     │
│                          │ 50×, causing 304 slope changes; Gen 9's uncapped variant showed the same failure); (2) a  │
│                          │ trend-lock/hysteresis mechanism on the velocity state: the estimated slope is only        │
│                          │ allowed to flip sign if it exceeds a noise-derived significance threshold (multiplied by  │
│                          │ an online estimate of slope uncertainty), directly attacking false reversals and slope    │
│                          │ churn; (3) velocity is shrunk toward its EMA in low-innovation regimes so noise cannot    │
│                          │ leak into the slope state; (4) a light 3-tap post-smoother (Gen current's trick) further  │
│                          │ suppresses spurious reversals with negligible phase delay. The output contract (len(x) -  │
│                          │ window_size + 1, warmup on first window-1 samples) is preserved exactly.                  │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
