│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ hybrid_quadfit_kalman_gate                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Crossover of the two best-performing implementations. From the current program (score     │
│                          │ 0.54) I keep the exponentially-weighted robust local quadratic regression evaluated at    │
│                          │ the window end (zero phase lag, best accuracy: avg_error 0.28, correlation 0.94, noise    │
│                          │ reduction 0.57), but now I also retain the fitted local slope b for each window. From the │
│                          │ Kalman/Holt inspiration program (lowest slope_changes 140.8 and false_reversals 114.6) I  │
│                          │ take the slope-gated reversal-suppression stage: a median filter on the estimated slope   │
│                          │ with a gate derived from local slope noise, followed by reintegration blended convexly    │
│                          │ (0.75/0.25) with the level-anchored regression output to prevent integrator drift.        │
│                          │ Finally, a light 3-tap smoothing pass plus a small slope-based forward extrapolation      │
│                          │ (lag_steps=1, using the quadratic fit's own slope, which is less noisy than the Kalman    │
│                          │ slope) compensates residual group delay without amplifying noise. This hybrid targets the │
│                          │ weaknesses of each parent: the regression parent's relatively high                        │
│                          │ slope_changes/false_reversals, and the Kalman parent's high lag/avg error.                │
