                        Patch Metadata - Gen 27/100 - Novelty: 1/3 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/3                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ pre_convolution_median_snap                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Add a second noise-scaled median snap applied to the raw input before the                 │
│                          │ convolution-based weighted regression. The current algorithm only snaps the output after  │
│                          │ convolution; noise-sized sample-to-sample steps in the raw signal still leak through the  │
│                          │ window average. Applying a 5-tap median filter to the input (with noise-scale detection)  │
│                          │ removes impulse-like noise spikes before the window averaging, compounding the smoothing  │
│                          │ effect on the output (targeting smoothness, currently 0.08) at negligible computational   │
