│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ kalman_quad_adaptive_mediansnap                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ The best prior variant (combined 0.54) was the innovation-adaptive Kalman prefilter       │
│                          │ followed by robust exponentially-weighted local quadratic regression evaluated at the     │
│                          │ window end — it achieved correlation 0.93-0.94 and noise_reduction 0.50-0.57, far better  │
│                          │ than the current trend-lock design (0.34 noise reduction, 0.53 combined). The current     │
│                          │ trend-lock hysteresis over-suppresses dynamics, hurting responsiveness and noise          │
│                          │ reduction. This edit replaces the trend-lock core with that proven pipeline, then adds a  │
│                          │ NEW final stage: a locally adaptive median-snap on output differences. Small              │
│                          │ point-to-point differences that deviate little from a rolling median of diffs are snapped │
│                          │ to the median, which removes residual jitter (slope churn / false reversals) without a    │
│                          │ global threshold — noisy non-stationary segments get aggressive snapping via a rolling    │
│                          │ MAD-of-diffs, clean segments keep their dynamics. This directly targets slope_changes and │
│                          │ false_reversals (the multi-objective smoothness terms) while the quadratic fit's t=0      │
│                          │ evaluation keeps phase lag near zero, and the Kalman slope state preserves                │
│                          │ responsiveness.                                                                           │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0338                                                                                   │
