│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ capped_nis_kalman_sg                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Builds on the best prior program (combined 0.58: adaptive Kalman + Savitzky-Golay +       │
│                          │ weighted window mean, 41 slope changes, 36.6 false reversals). Its weakness is the        │
│                          │ unbounded NIS-driven process-noise multiplier `q_scale = q_base*(1+10*min(nis,50)/10)`    │
│                          │ which can inflate Q to 51×q_base, leaking noise into the velocity state and causing       │
│                          │ spurious reversals. New configuration: (1) cap the multiplier at 4× (`q_scale =           │
│                          │ q_base*min(1.0+nis/10.0, 4.0)`), (2) raise q_base from 0.01 to 0.02 so genuine turns      │
│                          │ still track, (3) add a slope median gate that suppresses small slope sign flips (kills    │
│                          │ false reversals, the metric that best predicts rank), (4) add mild forward extrapolation  │
│                          │ via the Kalman slope state to cut lag error. This keeps the smoothness/reversal advantage │
│                          │ while recovering tracking accuracy and lag.                                               │
