│ patch_name               │ dual_median_snap_prefilter                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ A fundamentally different architecture: instead of a single post-convolution noise gate,  │
│                          │ this design applies noise-scaled median snapping twice — once before and once after the   │
│                          │ exponential window convolution. The pre-convolution snap removes noise-sized steps from   │
│                          │ the raw signal so the windowed average operates on already-debiased data, compounding the │
│                          │ smoothing effect on the output. The mechanism remains entirely in the level domain (no    │
│                          │ slope gating), which prior generations showed is strictly superior. By quantizing         │
│                          │ noise-sized deviations to the local median before averaging, the exponential convolution  │
│                          │ receives a cleaner input, reducing spurious slope changes at the output without adding    │
│                          │ lag, since median snapping is zero-phase and O(1) per sample with a small 5-tap window.   │
│                          │ This targets smoothness improvement while lag and tracking remain governed by the same    │
│                          │ window length, preserving responsiveness.                                                 │
