│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ savitzky_golay_with_recency_tilt                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the per-sample Kalman + Holt cascade (which incurs lag on trend segments and only │
│                          │ achieves 0.33 noise reduction / 103 slope changes) with a vectorized Savitzky-Golay       │
│                          │ (order-2 polynomial) FIR smoother convolved with an exponentially decaying                │
│                          │ recency-weighting kernel (e^-1.5 tilt). The polynomial fit preserves local trend dynamics │
│                          │ (low lag, good tracking), the recency tilt shifts effective weight toward the most recent │
│                          │ samples to cut group delay, and the convolution is fully vectorized via np.convolve       │
│                          │ "valid" mode preserving the 1.00 efficiency score. A post-pass zero-phase slope gate      │
│                          │ suppresses noise-induced false reversals by detecting slope sign flips smaller than a     │
│                          │ local noise threshold and re-integrating the gated slopes. This directly targets          │
│                          │ slope_changes (103), false_reversals (85.4), and lag_error (0.42) simultaneously.         │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0092                                                                                   │
