│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ cap_nis_q_and_stronger_postsmooth                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ False reversals (85.2) and slope changes (108.2) are the dominant score drivers; prior    │
│                          │ data shows programs under ~60 reversals score ≥0.57. The current Kalman pre-filter        │
│                          │ inflates process noise by up to 50×r when NIS spikes (q_dyn = r * min(nis-1, 50)), which  │
│                          │ leaks measurement noise directly into the slope state and produces spurious directional   │
│                          │ reversals. Capping the dynamic inflation at 3×r (and reducing its coupling into the slope │
│                          │ state from 0.25 to 0.1) keeps the velocity estimate clean while still allowing genuine    │
│                          │ turns to be tracked via the baseline Q. To further cut noise-induced reversals at         │
│                          │ negligible phase cost, the 5-tap binomial post-smoother is extended to a 7-tap binomial   │
│                          │ kernel (zero-phase interior, still near-zero lag). This trades a tiny amount of           │
│                          │ responsiveness for a large reduction in false reversals and slope changes, which the      │
│                          │ metric rankings show is the highest-value exchange.                                       │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0270                                                                                   │
