│ patch_name               │ larger_sg_window_sweep                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Per the Gen 32 finding, the steeper e^-1.5 tilt paired with the 2W-1 window held the 0.62 │
│                          │ score, and the sensitivity note suggests larger SG windows may buy additional smoothness  │
│                          │ (slope_changes and false_reversals are the weakest metrics) at a lag cost that the        │
│                          │ recency-weighted convolution may recover. I sweep the SG window from 2W-1 to 2W+3 with    │
│                          │ order-2 polynomials, keeping the proven e^-1.5 recency tilt and all convolution           │
│                          │ vectorized. The quadratic fit and recency weighting should absorb the extra group delay   │
│                          │ while the wider window further suppresses noise-induced slope reversals.                  │
