│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ adaptive_local_snap_threshold                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the global MAD-of-diffs sigma in the slope-consistency pass with a locally        │
│                          │ adaptive, vectorized rolling robust sigma computed over ±25-sample blocks of x_smooth     │
│                          │ diffs via sliding_window_view. Noisy non-stationary segments get aggressive snapping      │
│                          │ (smaller local sigma → more median blending) while clean segments with genuine dynamics   │
│                          │ get a larger local sigma and keep their full response. This directly targets lag_error    │
│                          │ (0.41) and avg_error (0.51) without sacrificing the reversal/slope gains (30 slope        │
│                          │ changes). Since the diff series of x_smooth is short-window available, we pad edge blocks │
│                          │ via reflection to keep lengths aligned. The blend is slightly increased (0.5 → 0.6) for   │
│                          │ snapped samples to strengthen noise suppression where local noise dominates, exploiting   │
│                          │ the responsiveness margin (0.71).                                                         │
