│ patch_name               │ locally_adaptive_threshold_tuning                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The locally adaptive σ threshold is already implemented but is applied at 0.5σ —          │
│                          │ identical to the previous global constant, so its adaptivity isn't exploited.             │
│                          │ Responsiveness (0.71) has the most headroom of all sub-scores while lag_error remains     │
│                          │ 0.41. Raising the snap threshold to 0.7× local σ and strengthening the median blend (0.6  │
│                          │ med / 0.4 y) means noisy non-stationary segments (large local σ) get aggressively snapped │
│                          │ toward the running median — killing spurious slope reversals and reducing lag-inducing    │
│                          │ dither — while clean segments (small local σ) keep essentially untouched dynamics. Since  │
│                          │ the threshold now scales with local noise, raising the multiplier does not sacrifice      │
│                          │ genuine trend changes the way raising the old global threshold would. This directly       │
│                          │ targets lag_error and slope_changes while keeping the false-reversal advantage, and stays │
│                          │ fully vectorized (efficiency 1.00 preserved).                                             │
