│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ local_adaptive_snap_threshold                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the fixed 5-tap binomial post-smoothing with a locally adaptive "snap" stage. The │
│                          │ key weakness (lag_error 0.33, slope_changes 108) comes from globally applying a smoothing │
│                          │ kernel: clean dynamic segments get over-smoothed (lag) while noisy segments may still     │
│                          │ jitter. Instead: (1) compute robust local noise scale σ via sliding_window_view on the    │
│                          │ diff of the pre-filtered signal (fully vectorized, efficiency stays ~1.00); (2) where     │
│                          │ consecutive output differences are below the local threshold (0.5·σ), snap them toward    │
│                          │ the local median slope (aggressive de-jitter in noisy segments); (3) where diffs exceed   │
│                          │ the threshold (genuine dynamics), leave them untouched (no added lag). This preserves     │
│                          │ responsiveness (0.75 has margin) while cutting spurious slope changes and false           │
│                          │ reversals.                                                                                │
