│ patch_description        │ Implements the recommended controlled mutation: a constant-velocity Kalman prefilter with │
│                          │ NIS-driven process noise where `q_base = 0.02 * r` and the multiplier is hard-capped at   │
│                          │ 4× (previously up to 51×), so noise can no longer flood the velocity state — the likely   │
│                          │ driver of the 165.8 slope changes / 125.8 false reversals. The Kalman output is followed  │
│                          │ by the leading-edge exponentially-weighted regression (zero group delay, preserving the   │
│                          │ excellent lag 0.31 / responsiveness 0.76 of the current program), then a slope-EMA        │
│                          │ trend-lock and a stronger locally-adaptive hysteresis snap (k=0.8, blend=0.75) to remove  │
│                          │ residual slope churn. This combination directly attacks slope_changes and false_reversals │
│                          │ while keeping the responsiveness backbone validated in earlier gens.                      │
