│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_trend_lock_slope_damping_stage                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ The dominant scoring weakness is slope churn (slope_changes=167.8, false_reversals=127.4) │
│                          │ while accuracy is already high. The best prior program (combined 0.58) achieved           │
│                          │ slope_changes=41 and false_reversals=36 via implicit slope damping (Kalman velocity state │
│                          │ + Savitzky-Golay). I port that mechanism into this pipeline as an explicit, cheap         │
│                          │ "trend-lock" stage: the leading-edge fit already computes per-window slopes; I return     │
│                          │ them, then apply EMA shrinkage-smoothing of the slope sequence and adjust the output      │
│                          │ level by the slope disagreement. Because the level estimate y is already evaluated at the │
│                          │ window's leading edge (zero group delay), this damping adds almost no lag (lag_error      │
│                          │ stays ~0.3) while suppressing noise-induced directional reversals — exactly the trade the │
│                          │ best prior program exploited. Additionally, I tighten Stage 3 slightly (k 0.5→0.65) since │
│                          │ the trend-lock stage will do most of the reversal killing. All stages remain              │
│                          │ vectorized/O(n), preserving efficiency_score=1.0.                                         │
│ num_applied              │ 3                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0220                                                                                   │
