│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ vectorize_median_snap                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ The pipeline's only remaining Python-level loop is the 5-tap running median snap          │
│                          │ (`np.median(pad) for i in range(len(y))`). Replacing it with `sliding_window_view` + a    │
│                          │ single vectorized `np.median(..., axis=1)` computes identical numerics (same edge         │
│                          │ padding, same 5-sample windows, same median operation) while removing O(n) interpreter    │
│                          │ overhead and eliminating the fragile per-index bounds-checking pattern that multi-stage   │
│                          │ pipelines carry as a crash risk. This is a strictly-safe mutation: every metric-earning   │
