│ patch_description        │ The current NIS-driven adaptation allows q_scale to reach up to 51× baseline (q_base * (1 │
│                          │ + 10*min(nis,50)/10) = 0.01 * 51), injecting excessive process noise into the velocity    │
│                          │ state. This noise propagates through the SG window and the median-snap pass, and is a     │
│                          │ likely contributor to the residual slope changes and false reversals. Softening the       │
│                          │ adaptation — capping q_scale at 4× and raising q_base from 0.01 to 0.02 — keeps the       │
│                          │ filter adaptive to genuine dynamics changes while suppressing noise-driven responsiveness │
│                          │ spikes. Responsiveness (0.71) has margin to absorb slightly heavier smoothing, and        │
│                          │ improved noise reduction should raise correlation, smoothness, and accuracy, which        │
│                          │ dominate the combined score.                                                              │
