│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ dual_stage_kalman_irwls_reversal_gate                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Structural redesign around a single causal core: a constant-velocity Kalman filter that   │
│                          │ exposes BOTH its level and slope estimates, eliminating the multi-pass pipeline           │
│                          │ (Savitzky-Golay → window average → median snap → trend-lock) that over-smoothed and drove │
│                          │ lag_error to 0.46, avg_error to 0.56, and correlation down to 0.74. The new architecture: │
│                          │ (1) Kalman level+slope states give noise-reduced, near-zero-lag output directly; (2) a    │
│                          │ vectorized iteratively-reweighted (IRLS, Huber) Savitzky-Golay polish runs once on the    │
│                          │ Kalman level (robust to residual outliers, preserves polynomial trends); (3) a predictive │
│                          │ slope-extrapolation blend in high-NIS regimes adds responsiveness at genuine turning      │
│                          │ points (fixes lag without adding false reversals); (4) a statistically-gated reversal     │
│                          │ hysteresis on output diffs only rejects sign flips insignificant w.r.t. local MAD of      │
│                          │ diffs — one final, principled stage instead of the stacked snap stages. Overall the data  │
│                          │ flow goes from 5 cascaded smoothers (each adding lag/distortion) to 2 smoothing           │
│                          │ operations plus adaptive prediction, restoring correlation (0.93 in the top prior         │
│                          │ programs) and accuracy while keeping slope_changes/false_reversals low.                   │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
