│ patch_description        │ The recommendation identifies bidirectional Kalman fusion as the only untested structural │
│                          │ addition that was never implicated in prior failures. I preserve the champion cascade     │
│                          │ (adaptive-Q Kalman → robust SG → recency convolution → median snap) and add a single      │
│                          │ structural mutation at Stage 1: run the adaptive-Q Kalman both forward and on the         │
│                          │ time-reversed input, then fuse the two estimates 50/50. The forward pass has zero phase   │
│                          │ lag at the start but accumulates endpoint-phase error; the backward pass has the opposite │
│                          │ bias; averaging cancels much of the interior phase error, potentially lifting tracking    │
│                          │ accuracy while leaving the downstream smoothness stages untouched. All previously failed  │
│                          │ paradigms (slope-domain rewriting, endpoint regression, sign-locking) are avoided.        │
