│ patch_description        │ The largest remaining metric gap is noise_reduction (0.34 vs historical 0.59). No         │
│                          │ existing cascade stage improves it, so I add the recommended Stage 3.5: a 5-tap median    │
│                          │ snap applied directly to `x_smooth` (the robust-SG output) before the recency-weighted    │
│                          │ convolution. The snap computes edge-padded 5-tap medians via `sliding_window_view` +      │
│                          │ `np.median(axis=1)`, then blends 50/50 only where the local step size falls below 0.5×    │
│                          │ the robust local-σ threshold (MAD-of-diffs), exactly mirroring the validated final snap   │
│                          │ mechanism. This suppresses residual amplitude noise on the smoothed track without         │
│                          │ disturbing the validated Kalman/SG/recency stages, reducing residual variance against the │
│                          │ clean signal (noise_reduction) while keeping genuine steps (which exceed the threshold)   │
│                          │ intact. All other stages, I/O conventions, and function signatures are unchanged.         │
