│ patch_name               │ fix_despike_and_two_scale_sg                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ The current program has a structural defect: `_impulse_despike` was accidentally nested   │
│                          │ *inside* `adaptive_filter`, so it is not reachable at module level (a latent NameError    │
│                          │ path), and `adaptive_filter` retains an O(n·W) Python loop. Fix 1 relocates the despike   │
│                          │ to module scope and vectorizes the baseline moving average via cumsum.                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Fix 2 targets the two weakest metrics — noise_reduction (0.33) and slope_changes (42.6) — │
│                          │ without touching the validated five-stage structure or the (window, tilt) output          │
│                          │ convention: (a) cap the Kalman adaptive process-noise multiplier at 4x (the champion's    │
│                          │ cap, which reduced slope changes), and (b) add a second, coarser zero-phase               │
│                          │ Savitzky-Golay pass (order 2, odd window, length-clamped with the same defensive edge     │
│                          │ clamps that kept the champion's 100% validation rate). SG is zero-phase, so extra         │
│                          │ smoothing costs no lag error, but it directly increases noise reduction and fewer         │
│                          │ residual slope reversals.                                                                 │
