│ patch_description        │ Add a Stage 3.5 pre-convolution 5-tap median snap on x_smooth to attack noise_reduction   │
│                          │ (0.33, the largest remaining gap; family-wide 0.31-0.35 vs Gen 13's historical 0.59).     │
│                          │ Compute edge-padded 5-tap medians of x_smooth via sliding_window_view +                   │
│                          │ np.median(axis=1), apply the validated 0.5× local-σ threshold on step sizes, blend        │
│                          │ 0.5/0.5 exactly like the proven Stage 5 mechanism, and feed the result into the recency   │
│                          │ convolution. Median filtering is optimal for removing impulsive residual noise that       │
│                          │ survives the SG stage while preserving monotonic trend segments (edge-preserving), so it  │
│                          │ reduces residual variance (noise_reduction) without adding phase delay or perturbing the  │
│                          │ validated Kalman/SG/recency stages.                                                       │
