│ patch_description        │ Restructures the filter around a two-pass capped-NIS Kalman smoother: a forward adaptive  │
│                          │ Kalman run fused 50/50 with a time-reversed backward run, stitching the first half from   │
│                          │ the forward pass and the second half from the backward pass to reduce endpoint-phase      │
│                          │ error in the interior. The previous SG/convolution-style weighted quadratic regression is │
│                          │ replaced by a constant-acceleration Kalman model with adaptive measurement noise          │
│                          │ (innovation-gated, capped NIS) which handles non-stationarity online. Downstream, the     │
│                          │ slope-gated reversal suppression and light 3-tap smoothing are retained (they were not    │
│                          │ implicated in prior regressions) and reorganized into a small modular pipeline. Backward  │
│                          │ pass is implemented by simple reversal of the input (no index arithmetic beyond           │
│                          │ np.concatenate / reversal), matching the recommended approach.                            │
