│ patch_name               │ wavelet_trend_fusion_filter                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ A fundamentally different approach: replace the Kalman+SG pipeline with multi-scale       │
│                          │ wavelet trend fusion. The signal is decomposed via à trous (stationary) wavelet           │
│                          │ transform, noise-dominated detail scales are soft-thresholded (Stein-style, robust        │
│                          │ MAD-scaled) while signal-bearing scales are kept, and the reconstruction is fused with a  │
│                          │ robust local-linear (Theil–Sen-like) trend estimate. Because à trous wavelets are         │
│                          │ zero-phase (no group delay at any scale), lag is structurally minimal — no                │
│                          │ recency-weighted de-lag convolution is needed. Trend-preserving reconstruction with       │
│                          │ per-scale adaptive thresholds attacks spurious slope reversals (the dominant score        │
│                          │ limiter) directly, while keeping mid-frequency dynamics for tracking accuracy. Final pass │
│                          │ is a predictive local polynomial extrapolation-shifted median smoother (low-order,        │
│                          │ edge-corrected) to suppress residual churn without phase delay.                           │
