│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ widen_sg_window_and_steepen_tilt                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ The current program (0.63) pairs SG smoothing with a final exponential-weight convolution │
│                          │ tilt of e^-1.0. Prior sweeps showed the smoothness-lag frontier plateau breaks only when  │
│                          │ the SG window and the exponential tilt steepness move together as a matched pair:         │
│                          │ widening SG to 2W+7 with tilt e^-1.2 gave +0.04 smoothness and -5 reversals for only      │
│                          │ +0.02 lag. Extending the frontier further, SG window to 2W+11 with tilt steepened to      │
│                          │ e^-1.0 keeps the pair matched: the wider SG window suppresses residual level-domain       │
│                          │ variance (improving both smoothness and noise_reduction), while the steeper exponential   │
│                          │ weighting compensates by emphasizing recent samples and shaving phase lag. The `sg_win >  │
│                          │ len(x_kalman)` clamp and valid-mode convolution must be preserved exactly so short inputs │
│                          │ stay safe and output length stays n-W+1. Window and tilt must move together (Gen 63       │
│                          │ showed destructive interaction when they diverge).                                        │
