│ patch_description        │ False reversals remain the strongest rank predictor of the combined score (21.2 → 0.64;   │
│                          │ 23–26 → 0.62–0.63; 28+ → 0.58). The current Gen uses a 0.7σ step threshold with a 0.6     │
│                          │ median blend. The recommendation is to co-sweep the Stage 5 snap parameters as an atomic  │
│                          │ pair: lower the threshold to k=0.45 (catching more sub-noise steps before they become     │
│                          │ sign flips) while raising the blend to 0.75 (removing those flagged steps more            │
│                          │ completely). The sign-hysteresis mask logic stays byte-identical — Gen 70's mechanism     │
│                          │ design is validated; only the permissiveness/completeness balance is untested. Prior      │
│                          │ generations show that adding new damping mechanisms (Gen 66/67) fails, so we tune this    │
│                          │ existing mechanism instead. The threshold feeds both Pass 1 and Pass 2 (both reference    │
│                          │ `thr`), so a single constant change propagates consistently; the Pass 2 snap blend is     │
│                          │ also tuned to complete the removal more aggressively. Lower lag risk is bounded since     │
│                          │ genuine trend steps still exceed 0.45σ locally and remain untouched.                      │
