│ patch_description        │ Crossover of the two pipelines, which differ only in Stage 6 (ZeroPhasePolishStage). The  │
│                          │ current program already slightly outperforms the prior baseline (slope_changes 24.2 vs    │
│                          │ 24.6, false_reversals 21.0 vs 21.4), so I keep the full current program and strengthen    │
│                          │ the weakest metrics (noise_reduction 0.33, smoothness 0.45) without sacrificing lag or    │
│                          │ accuracy. The crossover keeps: (1) the robust MAD noise estimator, (2) the capped-NIS     │
│                          │ adaptive Kalman, (3) the widened (2W+7) iterative-reweighted SG co-swept with the e^-1.2  │
│                          │ recency tilt, (4) the pre-convolution median snap, (5) the local hysteresis snap, and (6) │
│                          │ the zero-phase SG polish — which adds no group delay, hence targets                       │
│                          │ noise_reduction/smoothness while preserving the improved slope-change/false-reversal      │
│                          │ numbers. A small tweak: replace the noisy `np.median(np.abs(windows - median))` style     │
│                          │ rolling ops with streamlined sliding_window_view code, and apply the median snap twice    │
│                          │ (pre- and post-recency) via the same vectorized helper for extra impulsive-noise          │
│                          │ suppression at O(n) cost. Execution time remains well within budget.                      │
