│ patch_description        │ Implements the recommended matched co-move: widen the Savitzky-Golay window to 2W+11 and  │
│                          │ steepen the recency-weight tilt to e^-1.0 as a pair. The prior (2W+7, e^-1.2) sweep was   │
│                          │ the only configuration that broke the 0.62 plateau (+0.04 smoothness, −5 reversals for    │
│                          │ only +0.02 lag), and generational history confirms window and tilt must move together or  │
│                          │ the interaction turns destructive. The wider SG window suppresses residual level          │
│                          │ variance, co-targeting smoothness and noise reduction, while the slightly gentler tilt    │
│                          │ (e^-1.0 vs e^-1.2) keeps lag error nearly unchanged. The Kalman pre-filter (soft          │
│                          │ NIS-capped), 5-tap median snap, and trend-lock reversal hysteresis are retained           │
│                          │ unchanged. The `sg_win > len(x_kalman)` clamp and valid-mode convolution are preserved    │
│                          │ exactly.                                                                                  │
