│ patch_name               │ bidir_kalman_staged_pipeline                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Crossover of the two top lineages: the staged coarse-to-fine pipeline (champion, 0.64 —   │
│                          │ noise estimator → capped-Q adaptive Kalman → robust widened SG → recency convolution →    │
│                          │ local hysteresis snap → zero-phase SG polish) crossed with the first program's structural │
│                          │ mutation: bidirectional Kalman fusion. The capped-Q adaptive Kalman is now run both       │
│                          │ forward and on the time-reversed signal and fused 50/50; the backward pass's phase error  │
│                          │ opposes the forward pass's, cancelling interior lag and improving tracking/lag at no      │
│                          │ smoothness cost — a mechanism the champion lineage never inherited. All downstream stages │
│                          │ (widened robust SG with co-swept recency tilt, hysteresis snap with sign-flip logic,      │
│                          │ zero-phase polish) are kept exactly as validated. The graded-blend pre-convolution median │
│                          │ snap from the last variant is also retained for its noise-reduction benefit. The only     │
│                          │ extra compute is one more O(n) Kalman pass, keeping efficiency ~1.0.                      │
