│ patch_description        │ The lineage's validated lesson is that structural Kalman pre-passes were worth +0.01 and  │
│                          │ that matched pairs of knobs must move together. Currently Stage 1 runs a single           │
│                          │ bidirectional adaptive-Kalman pass (q_base=0.01). I propose adding a second, *weaker*     │
│                          │ bidirectional Kalman pre-pass (q_base=0.005, i.e. half strength, per the recommendation   │
│                          │ of q_base = 0.005×r-scale regime) applied to the despiked signal *before* the existing    │
│                          │ Stage 1. The weak pre-pass strips the coarsest measurement noise so the main adaptive     │
│                          │ pass sees a cleaner innovation sequence; its NIS adaptation then spends its               │
│                          │ responsiveness budget on genuine dynamics changes rather than on noise bursts, which      │
│                          │ should reduce spurious slope reversals (false_reversals 13.0, slope_changes 14.6 are the  │
│                          │ biggest score drags) without adding group delay — bidirectional fusion keeps the interior │
│                          │ phase error near zero. Both stages move as a matched pair: pre-pass is deliberately       │
│                          │ half-strength so the main pass remains the dominant smoother, avoiding over-smoothing     │
│                          │ that would hurt lag_error and responsiveness.                                             │
