│                          │ capped-NIS adaptive Kalman → widened robust SG (2W+7) → recency-weighted convolution      │
│                          │ (tilt e^-1.2) → local hysteresis snap → zero-phase SG polish) and the validated Stage-3.5 │
│                          │ median snap, but combines the parents' snap parameters into an intermediate setting       │
│                          │ (k=0.5, blend=0.7) to balance noise-driven snapping aggressiveness against                │
│                          │ responsiveness. Additionally, the zero-phase polish window is widened from 7 to 9 taps    │
│                          │ (still short, symmetric, zero-phase) to attack the weakest metrics — noise_reduction      │
