│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_atrous_wavelet_shrinkage                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Add a B3-spline à-trous wavelet denoising stage with correct per-scale sigma calibration  │
│                          │ between the Kalman pre-filter and the SG smoother. Wavelet shrinkage at each scale uses   │
│                          │ thresholds proportional to the true noise gain at that scale (gain_j^2 = sum of squared   │
│                          │ kernel taps at dilation j), so coarser scales shrink proportionally more noise without    │
│                          │ biasing signal structure. This directly attacks noise_reduction (currently 0.34) while    │
│                          │ adding zero group delay (à-trous is a zero-phase, non-causal-in-analysis-but-symmetric    │
│                          │ transform on the buffered window) and improving correlation, since denoising prior to SG  │
│                          │ lets the SG window operate on a cleaner signal. The finest scale is soft-thresholded      │
│                          │ hardest; scales beyond ~log2(n) are kept (trend). Floor sigma at 1e-12 to avoid           │
│                          │ division-by-zero.                                                                         │
