│                          │ (0.88). The Gen 78 recommendation: in `_threshold_details`, the noise-dominated branch    │
│                          │ (mag < 0.5) currently applies soft-threshold then a mild 0.5× shrink, leaving residual    │
│                          │ noise in fine scales. Switch to full hard-thresholding: zero all coefficients below the   │
│                          │ universal threshold entirely (soft-threshold already gives exactly that for |c| < thr —   │
│                          │ the additional 0.5× multiplier is what leaves residual noise in surviving coefficients).  │
│                          │ Additionally tighten the threshold multiplier from 0.75 to 0.85 so more fine-scale noise  │
│                          │ is captured, while keeping signal-bearing scales untouched (zero-phase,                   │
│                          │ correlation-safe). The slope_changes/false_reversals metrics should also improve since    │
│                          │ residual fine-scale noise is what drives spurious reversals. Atomic co-sweep as           │
│                          │ recommended.                                                                              │
